  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Response Overview for the Sudan Crisis and Neighbouring Countries: Chad and Central African Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the onset of the conflict in Sudan in April 2023, more than 7.9 million people have been internally displaced within Sudan and more than 2.3 million people crossed borders into neighbouring countries, including Chad and the Central African Republic. This project is implemented in Chad and the Central African Republic to address the needs of populations affected by the crisis, including returnees and host communities. In Chad, this project aims to improve the resilience of vulnerable returnee and host community households through access to essential infrastructure and livelihoods in Ouadda&#xef; and Sila provinces. In the Central African Republic, this project supports relocated refugees and returnees through multisectoral assistance, including shelter and non-food items, protection, mental health and psychosocial support, and hygiene promotion activities in Vakaga, Bamingui-Bangoran and Ouaka prefectures. The project also ensures that the humanitarian community is informed on trends and flows of new arrivals in the Central African Republic, through the collection, analysis and sharing of data through the International Organization for Migration&#x2019;s Displacement Tracking Matrix.</narrative>
  </description>
